From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] qt-api: do not marshal invalid QVariant arguments

AbstractSensorChannelInterface::call() takes eight QVariant slots, all
defaulting to QVariant(), and forwards all of them to QDBusAbstractInterface.
Qt5 dropped trailing invalid ones; Qt6 refuses to marshal them:

    QDBusMarshaller: cannot add an invalid QVariant
    Marshalling failed: Invalid QVariant passed in arguments

So nearly every call from the client library fails before reaching sensord -
start(), setInterval(), the property accessors, all of them. On LuneOS this
shows up as the compositor creating a sensor session successfully and then
never receiving a reading, so the screen does not rotate; starting any other
sensor app makes the adaptor run and rotation begins working, which is a
confusing way for this to present. luna-surfacemanager logs 144 of these on
a single boot.

Pass only the arguments that were actually supplied.

Upstream-Status: Pending
--- a/qt-api/abstractsensor_i.cpp
+++ b/qt-api/abstractsensor_i.cpp
@@ -536,7 +536,22 @@
                                                   const QVariant& arg7,
                                                   const QVariant& arg8)
 {
-    return pimpl_->call(mode, method, arg1, arg2, arg3, arg4, arg5, arg6, arg7, arg8);
+    /*
+     * Qt6's QDBus refuses to marshal an invalid QVariant, where Qt5 silently
+     * dropped trailing ones. Every call here passes all eight slots, so any
+     * call with fewer real arguments - which is nearly all of them - fails with
+     * "Marshalling failed: Invalid QVariant passed in arguments" and never
+     * reaches sensord. Pass only the arguments that were actually given.
+     */
+    QList<QVariant> args;
+    const QVariant *const slots_[] = { &arg1, &arg2, &arg3, &arg4,
+                                       &arg5, &arg6, &arg7, &arg8 };
+    for (const QVariant *slot : slots_) {
+        if (!slot->isValid())
+            break;
+        args.append(*slot);
+    }
+    return pimpl_->callWithArgumentList(mode, method, args);
 }
 
 QDBusMessage AbstractSensorChannelInterface::callWithArgumentList(QDBus::CallMode mode, const QString& method,
